This crate is a Rust implementation of BiRefNet-lite's network, provided
under MIT, as the model is. It reproduces the results of the projects below,
measured by running them. The engines under it (crates/native-engine and
crates/native-vulkan) and the work they build on are credited in the
repository's NOTICE.

1. BiRefNet (MIT), by Peng Zheng, Dehong Gao, Deng-Ping Fan, Li Liu, Jorma
   Laaksonen, Wanli Ouyang and Nicu Sebe: "Bilateral Reference for
   High-Resolution Dichotomous Image Segmentation", CAAI Artificial
   Intelligence Research, 2024. https://github.com/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet
   The network, its weights (ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet_lite, MIT, Copyright (c)
   2024 ZhengPeng) and the reference outputs it is checked against.
   tools/birefnet/quantization_study.py restates the forward pass of BiRefNet's
   DeformableConv2d with rounded weights. No weights are included:
   tools/birefnet/export_weights.py converts an ONNX export of them that you obtain
   yourself, and the weights files it writes stay under the model's MIT
   licence (notice A), whose text has to travel with any of them you
   redistribute.

2. Swin Transformer (MIT), by Ze Liu, Yutong Lin, Yue Cao, Han Hu, Yixuan
   Wei, Zheng Zhang, Stephen Lin and Baining Guo, Microsoft: the backbone.
   https://github.com/microsoft/Swin-Transformer
   Deformable convolution v2 as torchvision's deform_conv2d computes it
   (BSD-3-Clause): Xizhou Zhu, Han Hu, Stephen Lin and Jifeng Dai,
   "Deformable ConvNets v2", CVPR 2019. https://github.com/pytorch/vision


A. BiRefNet, https://github.com/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet, the licence of its weights

